# [xihanzu-NR]
# Scratch worklogs, never part of the project.
.worksprint.md
.worksprint2.md

# Review notes and audit output. Kept out of the repository for the same reason
# the worklogs are: they are someone's working opinion about the code, not part
# of what the project ships. Both spellings are covered — `.review*.md` for a
# hidden working copy, `REVIEW*.md` for the readable one at the project root.
.review*.md
REVIEW*.md

# Dependencies. NOTE: without this, `git add -A` stages every dependency in the
# repository — there are example projects and a plugin each with their own
# node_modules, so a careless `add -A` offers ~28,000 files and 3.5M lines. It was
# missing before and this file is the fix.
node_modules/

# Build output.
dist/
compiler-rs/target/
target/

# Generated route table. Written by `hydra build` and `hydra routes` from the
# .hyx files under the pages directory; committing it means it can disagree with
# the folder it describes, which is the one thing generating it prevents.
.hydra/

# Generated type declarations. These are produced by `hydra types` from the
# source; committing them means they can disagree with the component they
# describe, which is the one thing the generator exists to prevent.
*.hyx.d.ts
*.hsx.d.ts
*.hys.d.ts

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode-test/

# A project's secrets. `.env.example` is committed (it has no values); every
# other shape holds values that must never reach a repository.
#
# `.env.local` and `.env.production.local` are what people type first — they are
# the Next/Vite convention — and leaving only `.env` here meant `git add -A`
# staged a file full of keys. `PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the client bundle, so
# the whole file is a secret, not just the unprefixed half.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Packed tarballs from `npm pack` / the pack-install check.
*.tgz

# editor extension build artifacts
*.vsix
editors/**/out/

# One lockfile. `bun.lock` sat beside `package-lock.json` while every workflow
# ran `npm ci`, so one of them was always stale and nothing said which. npm is
# what CI, the release and the install check use, so npm is the one kept.
bun.lock
watch-out/
